/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  chemistry/Glu-formation.dat -- the first 2 dissociations of L-glutamic acid, written from the master:
      H2Glu  <=>  Glu + 2 H+
  Made by bin/curate/species_c373.py from data/curation/batches/species_c373/*.tsv.

  logK25 and dH are the PRINTED values of the sources below (standard state ideal solution at 1 mol/kg, 298.15 K):
      pK1 = 2.162, dH1 = -0.27 kJ/mol
      pK2 = 4.272, dH2 = 1.56 kJ/mol
      pK3 = 9.93, dH3 = 40.07 kJ/mol
  Source: Miller & Smith-Magowan, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 19 (1990) 1049; H+(aq) = 0, zero ionic strength, aqueous species at 1 mol/dm3 (Table 1 caption, p. 1052).
  The master is H2Glu, the form a case declares; this record carries steps 2 to 3 (the sign flips with the direction written).
  The constant-dCp term of the printed dCp is NOT carried: the record grammar has no place for it (a
  van't Hoff integral with a constant dCp is exactly the `analytic` A1, A3, A4 terms; proposed, not done).
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType aqueousSpeciation;
schemaVersion 1;

species Glu; masters ( { ion H2Glu; nu 1; } { ion H; nu -2; } );
      logK25 -14.202; dH 41630; source "Miller & Smith-Magowan, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 19 (1990) 1049 -- Table 6, p. 1057: pK2 4.272, dH2 1.56 kJ/mol (read from a page image), pK3 9.93, dH3 40.07 kJ/mol (read from a page image) (pK, dH_ion at 298.15 K)";
